  "alternatives": [],
  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Hympavzi (marstacimab-hncq), a tissue factor pathway inhibitor (TFPI) antagonist for routine prophylaxis. Version: 1; Original: 11/12/2024; Accepted: 01/17/2025; Effective: 03/1/2025.",
    "Encoded: two closed hemophilia A/B indications without the respective factor inhibitors, age ≥12, hematologist or consultation, no prophylactic factor replacement combination, severe factor activity <1% OR at least 2 documented spontaneous joint bleeds, no breakthrough bleeding treatment, and new-start maintenance dosing ≤150 mg once weekly. Approval criteria 1-5 and denial criteria 1-4 are covered.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization approval up to 12 months.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 8 prefilled 150mg/ml syringes or pens per 28 days. max_units is null; quantity enforcement requires manual review.",
    "Cautions (notes only): thromboembolic events may occur; interrupt treatment if symptoms occur. Hympavzi may cause fetal harm.",
    "Remaining gaps: documentation verification, duration, reauthorization, quantity and cautions require manual review. PDL status unknown.",
    "Alternatives remain empty: Hemlibra is a hemophilia A prophylaxis peer, but its indication value differs and the evaluator does not translate indications between packs."
  ],
  "max_units": null,
